From 949e1039beecef26bb94b737b019b21b60116fe3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chromium Extend <noreply@localhost>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 21:58:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/31] Stop uploading form structure to the Autofill
 crowdsourcing server

Autofill uploads the structure of forms it encounters - field signatures, types, and page signatures - to content-autofill.googleapis.com, where it feeds Google field-classification heuristics. Local autofill does not depend on it.

kAutofillServerCommunication now defaults to disabled. This is the mechanism Chromium already provides for the purpose: AutofillCrowdsourcingManager::IsEnabled() returns false and every query and upload request returns early, with no error path and no logging.

Verified on device: browser launches clean, no crashes.
---
 .../autofill/core/common/autofill_debug_features.cc      | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/components/autofill/core/common/autofill_debug_features.cc b/components/autofill/core/common/autofill_debug_features.cc
index 4fb9b840fa..636741db5b 100644
--- a/components/autofill/core/common/autofill_debug_features.cc
+++ b/components/autofill/core/common/autofill_debug_features.cc
@@ -127,7 +127,14 @@ BASE_FEATURE_PARAM(std::string,
 // autofill server API url up to the parent "directory" of the "query" and
 // "upload" resources.
 // i.e., https://other.autofill.server:port/tbproxy/af/
-BASE_FEATURE(kAutofillServerCommunication, base::FEATURE_ENABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
+//
+// De-Googled build: disabled by default. When enabled, Autofill uploads the
+// structure of forms it encounters (field signatures, types, and page
+// signatures) to content-autofill.googleapis.com to improve Google's field
+// classification heuristics. Local autofill does not depend on it -
+// AutofillCrowdsourcingManager::IsEnabled() returns false and every query and
+// upload request returns early, with no error path.
+BASE_FEATURE(kAutofillServerCommunication, base::FEATURE_DISABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
 
 // When set to a non-zero value, the value is attached as an experiment ID to
 // all predictions requests to the Autofill server, as if it were an active GWS
